{
  "$description": "DepoAudio design tokens, in three tiers: ref (ref.color: the canonical DepoStack primitives, exact hex from depo-stack/tokens/dist/depostack.tokens.json; ref.local: app-local primitives the canonical palette does not define), base (mode-independent roles: font stacks, the focus ring and the depo-stack/DESIGN.md type roles at workspace density) and semantic (the app's role names per theme, aliasing ref). Every color $value is a plain {reference} to a ref hex; translucency is structured data in $extensions[\"com.depoaudio\"] as {alpha} or {alpha, over} (a layer composited onto a ground), never a custom string. Dimensions are DTCG {value, unit} objects; font weights are numbers; type widths are % numbers with the unit in $extensions, as in the canonical file. Ink is plum-black on the vellum board and pale vellum on the night board; gold (#E8A33A) is a fill or mark, never text, and the ink on gold is plum-black (#20182A) in both themes. Selected states use an ink border on the quiet fill, never a gold tint. Every text pair is WCAG AAA (7:1; 4.5:1 only for large bold text on the pressed gold), checked in src/__tests__/brand-tokens.test.js. Semantic colors become `H S% L%` channels (consumed as hsl(var(--token))) unless the name starts with `color-` (full paint values for SVG/canvas). Regenerate CSS with `npm run tokens`.",
